WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.058
PostgreSQL FILTER attaches a condition directly to
an aggregate COUNT

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:11.943
star FILTER where diagnosis equals Pneumonia counts
only matching rows The

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:18.683
query is often easier to scan because the aggregate
and its condition appear together Run

00:00:18.709 --> 00:00:24.300
it and compare the result with the CASE version The
output should express the

00:00:24.313 --> 00:00:25.484
same business meaning
